---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'October 11, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`User Data Deletion Instructions — ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Meta/Facebook and third-party platform user data deletion instructions for Reelay Studio. Learn how to immediately wipe your local tokens and SQLite data."
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <div class="badge badge-brand">Platform Compliance Notice</div>
        <h1 class="legal-title">User Data Deletion Instructions</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Compliance: Meta Platform Terms & Google API Limited Use • Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <!-- Primary Meta Platform Disclosure -->
      <div class="compliance-box" id="meta-compliance">
        <h3 class="compliance-box-title">Official Meta Data Deletion Statement</h3>
        <p class="official-statement">
          <strong>"Reelay does not store your social account data on cloud servers. All account tokens and drafts reside entirely in your local SQLite database on your device. To delete all associated data, open Reelay Settings → Accounts → Disconnect, or delete your local profile folder located at <code>~/Library/Application Support/reelay</code>."</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>Overview: Why We Don't Hold Your Data</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike centralized social media SaaS dashboards that maintain multi-tenant cloud databases of user tokens, posts, and analytics, <strong>Reelay Studio is 100% local-first software</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not host or operate any central database containing your Facebook, Instagram, Threads, YouTube, or TikTok profile data, access tokens, or media drafts. Because your data never leaves your workstation, you maintain sovereign control over your information at all times.
        </p>

        <h2>Methods to Delete or Purge Your Data</h2>
        <p>You can completely delete your data using any of the methods outlined below:</p>

        <!-- Method 1 -->
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-header">
            <span class="step-badge">Method 1</span>
            <h3>In-App Account Disconnection (Instant Token & Cache Purge)</h3>
          </div>
          <p>This is the fastest method to remove external platform credentials:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Launch <strong>Reelay Studio</strong> on your desktop.</li>
            <li>Click the <strong>Settings</strong> icon (bottom-left gear icon or <code>Cmd+,</code> / <code>Ctrl+,</code>).</li>
            <li>Select the <strong>Accounts</strong> tab from the sidebar.</li>
            <li>Locate the account you wish to remove (e.g., Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok).</li>
            <li>Click the red <strong>"Disconnect"</strong> button.</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="action-result">
            <strong>What happens immediately:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>The desktop app contacts the provider's OAuth revocation endpoint to invalidate your active tokens.</li>
              <li>OAuth tokens and credentials are deleted immediately from your operating system's native secure keychain (macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager).</li>
              <li>Associated account metadata, tokens, and channel identifiers are deleted from your local SQLite database (<code>app.db</code>).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Method 2 -->
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-header">
            <span class="step-badge">Method 2</span>
            <h3>Complete Local Storage Deletion (Full Reset)</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            If you wish to wipe 100% of Reelay Studio's local data from your computer, including your SQLite database, video indexes, and Whisper transcripts, delete the application data directory:
          </p>

          <div class="os-box">
            <h4>macOS</h4>
            <p>Open Terminal or Finder and delete the following directory:</p>
            <pre><code>rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/reelay</code></pre>
            <p class="note">Alternatively in Finder: Press <code>Cmd + Shift + G</code>, paste <code>~/Library/Application Support/reelay</code>, and move the folder to Trash.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="os-box">
            <h4>Windows</h4>
            <p>Open PowerShell or File Explorer and delete the following directory:</p>
            <pre><code>Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "$env:APPDATA\reelay"</code></pre>
            <p class="note">Alternatively in File Explorer: Navigate to <code>%APPDATA%\reelay</code> and delete the folder.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="action-result">
            <strong>What happens immediately:</strong>
            <p>
              Your local SQLite database, custom presets, automation rules, and local cache are permanently deleted. Raw video files on your hard drive remain untouched in their original directories.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Method 3 -->
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-header">
            <span class="step-badge">Method 3</span>
            <h3>Revoking Permissions from Meta / Third-Party Platforms</h3>
          </div>
          <p>You can also revoke Reelay's access directly from the social platform interfaces at any time:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Facebook & Instagram:</strong> Go to <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings?tab=applications" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook Settings & Privacy → Settings → Apps and Websites</a>. Find <strong>Reelay</strong> and click <strong>Remove</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google & YouTube:</strong> Go to <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account Permissions</a>. Select <strong>Reelay Studio</strong> and click <strong>Remove Access</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>TikTok:</strong> Go to TikTok Mobile App → Profile → Settings & Privacy → Security & Permissions → Manage App Permissions → <strong>Reelay</strong> → <strong>Remove Access</strong>.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Data Deletion Confirmation & Compliance Assistance</h2>
        <p>
          Because Reelay does not store your account data on remote servers, no central server processing or waiting periods apply. Once you perform any of the steps above, your data is erased immediately.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are an app reviewer or creator requiring a formal written confirmation of data deletion for audit purposes, or if you need assistance, please contact our compliance team:
        </p>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <p><strong>Compliance & Data Protection:</strong> <a href="mailto:compliance@reelay.app">compliance@reelay.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>Privacy Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@reelay.app">privacy@reelay.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>Response Time:</strong> Within 24-48 business hours</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .compliance-box-title {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: #6ee7b7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .official-statement {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #f8fafc;
  }

  .official-statement code {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-elevated);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    color: #a5b4fc;
    font-size: 0.95em;
  }

  .method-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.75rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .method-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .step-badge {
    background-color: var(--brand);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .method-card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .action-result {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    background-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .action-result strong {
    color: #6ee7b7;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .action-result ul {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .os-box {
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    background-color: var(--color-surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .os-box h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .os-box pre {
    background-color: var(--color-black);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .os-box code {
    color: #38bdf8;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .os-box .note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .contact-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .contact-card p {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .contact-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
